    "items": [
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m01",
        "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
        "role": "field_engineer",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:14:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Hi Erkki, I'm at the site now. Changed the SFP on transmission node TRN-042.\nLink is up and alarms cleared, but traffic is still not coming back. Have you seen this before?"
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m02",
        "author": "Erkki Expert",
        "role": "expert",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:16:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Yes. Is this one of the older units?"
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m03",
        "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
        "role": "field_engineer",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:16:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Yes, installed around 2019 I think."
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m04",
        "author": "Erkki Expert",
        "role": "expert",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:18:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Ok. Don't trust the green link status on those.\nSometimes after changing the SFP the interface comes up normally, but the forwarding state doesn't recover correctly."
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m05",
        "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
        "role": "field_engineer",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:18:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "So another SFP?"
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m06",
        "author": "Erkki Expert",
        "role": "expert",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:19:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "No. Usually the SFP is fine.\nCheck whether the traffic counters are actually increasing. If they stay at zero even though the interface is UP, it's probably the issue I've seen before."
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m07",
        "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
        "role": "field_engineer",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:21:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Yes. Link UP. RX power looks normal. Counters basically zero."
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m08",
        "author": "Erkki Expert",
        "role": "expert",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:22:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "That's it.\nDisable the interface, wait a little, then enable it again. Don't reboot the whole unit unless that fails."
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m09",
        "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
        "role": "field_engineer",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:25:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Did that. Traffic is back 👍"
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m10",
        "author": "Erkki Expert",
        "role": "expert",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:25:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Good. These old units sometimes behave like this after an optical module replacement."
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m11",
        "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
        "role": "field_engineer",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:26:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Is this documented somewhere?"
      },
      {
        "type": "message",
        "id": "thread-001-m12",
        "author": "Erkki Expert",
        "role": "expert",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:27:00Z",
        "channel": "teams",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Not that I know of 😄\nWe've just learned it over the years."
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "assertion_id": "CA-0001",
        "to": "Erkki",
        "thread_id": "thread-001",
        "text": "Your TRN-042 tip: does it apply to TRN-087 too? Same model, installed 2018, different site.",
        "options": [
          {
